],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.1.stable, 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS 26.3\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a node gets reparented (either through reparent() or remove_child() and add_child()), it will skip its _process() call for that frame\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI've attached at minimal reproduction project.\nThere's one node that has a continues process counter that ticks up every process frame.\nThere's another node that gets the last process counter and sees if it is further than 1 away from the current process counter (meaning there was a skipped frame in the node).\n\nThe first node also has logic that reparents the second node when you press 0.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26037322/test.zip)\n\nPress 0 to trigger reparent.\n\nA print will appear afterwards showcasing the skipped frame.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117487/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}